.TH SETUP\-CHROOT 8 "November 2026" "kryx-linux" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
setup\-chroot \- safely mount API filesystems and chroot into a KryX/CRUX root
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B setup\-chroot
.RI [ target_root ]
.RI [ command " [" args ...\& ]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B setup\-chroot
prepares a mounted KryX or CRUX target root filesystem for chroot administration
by bind\-mounting
.IR /dev ,
.IR /dev/pts ,
.IR /proc ,
.IR /sys ,
.IR /run ,
and (when present on the host)
.IR /sys/firmware/efi/efivars ,
copying host
.I /etc/resolv.conf
(dereferencing symlinks) for working DNS inside the chroot, and launching a
clean chroot environment.
.PP
When called with no arguments,
.I target_root
defaults to
.I /mnt
and
.I command
defaults to
.B /bin/bash \-l
(matching stock CRUX
.BR setup\-chroot ).
Upon exit or interruption
.RB ( SIGINT / SIGTERM ),
all mounts created by
.B setup\-chroot
are unmounted automatically in reverse order.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.PP
.nf
setup\-chroot
setup\-chroot /mnt
setup\-chroot /mnt /bin/bash \-c "kpm doctor && kpm sync"
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR setup (8),
.BR setup\-kryx (8),
.BR setup\-repo (8),
.BR chroot (8)
